    "font" : "CMR10",
    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "for some t0, which we assume is zero appropriately translating f in time. Here the second equality follows from the time periodicity of uA(x,t). All the trajectories (solutions to (1.6)) converge to uA(t,x) in the pullback sense (as the initial time goes to minus infinity). This holds even for the 3D NSE with small forces, see [11]."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 9,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 72.0, 523.367, 540.004, 558.838 ],
    "font" : "CMR10",
    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "If spatial oscillations of f dominate the temporal oscillations, then (−∆)−1f(t,x) is the leading term in uA(t,x). However, in applications to convex integration, the non-diagonal interactions between building blocks result in errors of type"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
