    "bounding box" : [ 261.32, 500.255, 350.68, 517.54 ],
    "font" : "CMR10",
    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "f = PHdiv (w ⊗ w),"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 11,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 72.0, 465.286, 540.003, 499.159 ],
    "font" : "CMR10",
    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "where w is the velocity (or magnetic field) perturbation, which, for simplicity, is assumed to be a just a T-periodic in time building block. To control the size of the error ∆w, the perturbation has to be highly intermittent (with the intermittency dimension D < 1). Then it is easy to check that"
  }, {
